<title>FRANCE: Aznar says Spain hopes Italy in EMU from start.</title>
<headline>Aznar says Spain hopes Italy in EMU from start.</headline>
<dateline>MARSEILLE, France 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish Prime Minister Jose Maria Aznar said on Tuesday he hopes Italy will be included in a single European currency from the start.</p>
<p>In a news conference aired live by Reuters Financial Television Aznar said: &quot;Of course Spain wants Italy to participate from the first moment (in the single European currency.&quot;</p>
<p>He was speaking at a closing news conference at the two-day Franco-Spanish summit.</p>
<p>Aznar said Spain was in favour of as many countries as possible being incorporated in EMU from the first.</p>
<p>&quot;I want the core (of nations included in the first phase of EMU) to be as wide as possible,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
